# Python
venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
*.whl

# Environment & secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.cer
credentials*
secrets.*
# ...but app/secrets.py is source code (it loads env vars), not a credential
# file. A bare `secrets.*` matched it too and silently kept it out of the
# repository, which broke a deployment: local tests passed and the server
# could not import its own router.
!app/secrets.py

